age for Core Web Vitals, you’ve used software built by Addy Osmani. In this episode, I sit down with Addy and we talk about his path from building a web browser aged just 16 to becoming a director at Google. We discuss what he learned from building tools for millions of developers, Google’s engineering culture, and why he continued doing hands-on coding work as a manager. We also get into how he works with AI agents today, the risks of ‘cognitive surrender,’ his approach to ‘loop engineering,’ and why it’s good to develop skills in product management, go-to-market, and other areas.\n\n—\nBrought to you by:\n• Antithesis – verify your system’s correctness without human review or traditional integration tests – and avoid bugs or outages https://antithesis.com/pragmatic\n• Sentry – application monitoring software considered “not bad” by millions of developers https://sentry.io/pragmatic\n• Google Cloud Run – run your code and host LLMs directly on top of Google’s scalable infrastructure, without having to worry about managing infra. https://cloud.google.com/run?e=487548...\n \n—\nThe Pragmatic Engineer deepdives relevant for this episode:\n• What is loop engineering? https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n• Inside Google’s engineering culture https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n• How AI-assisted coding will change software engineering: hard truths https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n• Are AI agents actually slowing us down? https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n• How Claude Code is built https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.... \n• How Codex is built https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n• From IDEs to AI Agents with Steve Yegge https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n• Google’s engineering culture: the podcast https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n\n—\nWhere to find Addy Osmani:\n• X: https://x.com/addyosmani \n• LinkedIn:   / addyosmani   \n• Website: https://addyosmani.com \n\n—\nIn this episode, we cover:\n00:00 Intro\n02:50 Addy’s current workflow\n05:11 Addy’s path into tech\n15:04 Addy’s work on jQuery\n16:44 TodoMVC\n21:44 Getting hired at Google and working on Chrome\n27:17 Building dev tools\n40:15 Core Web Vitals\n45:42 Google’s engineering culture\n51:03 Addy’s career trajectory at Google\n57:55 The director role at Google\n1:01:40 Cognitive debt and cognitive surrender\n1:03:03 Working with agents\n1:05:52 Loop engineering\n1:12:55 The changing role of the software engineer\n1:18:15 How Addy uses AI in writing\n1:27:40 What’s next for Addy\n1:28:47 Career advice\n\n—\nSee the transcript and other references from the episode at https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer....\n\n—\nProduction and marketing by https://penname.co/.","commandRuns":[{"startIndex":935,"length":32,"onTap":{"innertubeCommand":{"clickTrackingParams":"CBUQ040EGAciEwiSvbSOiLqXAxUBrWUDHc2zFzxIk-O7lfHzo_7ZAcoBBDFFo9E=","commandMetadata":{"webCommandMetadata":{"url":"https://www.youtube.com/redirect?event=video_description\u0026redir_token=QUZZTVljRnZlLWNtczl3aXkxY3NmVWhQVHZxQXxBSTVJdTVzS1NUV0RZajk5a2UxY0NLTVdFN3M0YXR6NFhnYWh5SHM2eXNhOHhmU1liQ0doOXplbENBSEtPTlF3Rk9YNGlsS0w0V1c5WTNGdVM2REVaRnRZM3FOOHJ6bVNTb2R3\u0026q=https%3A%2F%2Fantithesis.com%2Fpragmatic\u0026v=2fyPnxKu8ZM","webPageType":"WEB_PAGE_TYPE_UNKNOWN","rootVe":83769}},"urlEndpoint":{"url":"https://www.youtube.com/redirect?event=video_description\u0026redir_token=QUZZTVljRnZlLWNtczl3aXkxY3NmVWhQVHZxQXxBSTVJdTVzS1NUV0RZajk5a2UxY0NLTVdFN3M0YXR6NFhnYWh5SHM2eXNhOHhmU1liQ0doOXplbENBSEtPTlF3Rk9YNGlsS0w0V1c5WTNGdVM2REVaRnRZM3FOOHJ6bVNTb2R3\u0026q=https%3A%2F%2Fantithesis.com%2Fpragmatic\u0026v=2fyPnxKu8ZM","target":"TARGET_NEW_WINDOW","nofollow":true}}}},{"startIndex":1058,"length":27,"onTap":{"innertubeCommand":{"clickTrackingParams":"CBUQ040EGAciEwiSvbSOiLqXAxUBrWUDHc2zFzxIk-O7lfHzo_7ZAcoBBDFFo9E=","commandMetadata":{"webCommandMetadata":{"url":"https://www.youtube.com/redirect?event=video_description\u0026redir_token=QUZZTVljRzh3SVpDLTFVS3BKVXFJdGV5b2lIa3xBSTVJdTVzLThQX